      "writtenOn": "2014-11-19T01:12:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no need to replace \u0027/\u0027 with \u0027\\\u0027 on windows when creating a file. This is all over the place in the updater so I read a bit more about it. Windows has always supported forward slashes as directory separators when using the Win API (It does\u0027t work on command line obviously) So it is safe to use forward slashes in new File() calls.",
